clean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/council/ap-codex.md:8:- **Search: supported with an important denominator qualification.** The 26 groups contain **145 possible earlier–later pairs**. Two could not be exercised because an item was missing; of the remaining 143, two searches missed, leaving 141/143. If the question is whether the complete system found every listed pair, it is 141/145. Either count exceeds 90%. The 11-member guidance group alone supplies 55 pairs, and only one group member is labeled a revision, so the result says much more about repeated reporting than revisions. [Search misses]( /Users/lchingen/hivemind/poc/data/clean-acceptance-2026-11-09/step2/search-misses.json)
clean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/council/ap-codex.md:9:- **Wrong merges: the reported pass is not supported by the stored verdicts.** The third reader marked X7, X22 and X49 `merge_acceptable: false`. Counting all three gives **3/57 = 5.3%**, above 2%; the reported 1/57 counts only the verdict labeled “wrong.” X7 combines three companies’ results; X49 adds a separate 100-million-user goal to an 18-million-user figure. X49 is debatable because the shared figure is present, but it cannot be silently counted as acceptable after the reader marked it false. The dev draws have the same issue: their third readers marked 15, 13 and 16 disputed merges unacceptable, including overlaps, while Claude reports one wrong per draw. [Fresh verdicts]( /Users/lchingen/hivemind/poc/data/clean-acceptance-2026-11-09/step2/merge-third-answer.json)
