clean-arch/STEP1-SOURCE-PROVENANCE-CENSUS.md:30:The [lineage replay](../poc/data/clean-step1-source-lineage-2026-11-07/review.html) covers the 163 bounded affected records and 200 non-overlapping feed articles selected by a recorded hash seed. An independent reader reran the actual current cleaner and verified the raw and cleaned records: all 363 outputs matched the saved cleaned text. Current HTML was available for 362 pages; the remaining page reproduced through the cleaner's existing no-HTML fallback. Current database and HTML-index hashes remained unchanged during the run. This establishes reproduction with the current saved inputs and extractor, not independent proof that every historical HTML byte is unchanged.
clean-arch/STEP1-SOURCE-PROVENANCE-CENSUS.md:32:Across 15,280 cleaned lines, 15,026 have one exact whole-line candidate in the captured page, 237 have multiple exact candidates, and 17 have a transformed joined-byline candidate. A single exact text candidate is a location observation; multiple candidates do not reveal which occurrence was retained, and a joined line is not a verbatim original line. The [raw lineage records](../poc/data/clean-step1-source-lineage-2026-11-07/lineage.jsonl) preserve the page and cleaned text, candidate positions, raw character offsets and extractor observations. A known citation is contiguous in cleaned text but not in the captured page; both sets of exact offsets are retained without changing the evidence.
clean-arch/STEP1-SOURCE-PROVENANCE-CENSUS.md:34:Among the 762 retained lines in the bounded components, 746 NVIDIA lines and two Cisco lines did not meet the cleaner's normalized extractor-text match and had its long-sentence shape; with a nonempty extractor result, that is consistent with the existing long-line retention fallback. Twelve TradingKey lines met the cleaner's extractor-text match. An extractor match checks normalized text, not authorship or semantic provenance. The nearest identified label was one nonempty captured-page line away on 158 affected pages, two on four and three on one. Distance is not evidence of a label's scope, and these three explicit structures do not cover arbitrary publishers. [Reproducible analysis](../poc/data/clean-step1-source-lineage-2026-11-07/analysis.json).
clean-arch/STEP1-SOURCE-PROVENANCE-CENSUS.md:36:The 200 additional selected articles contain 1,933,930 captured-page characters and 923,342 cleaned-text characters. Across these pages, the median captured page has 168.5 nonempty line positions without an exact or joined-byline candidate in the cleaned output. This is an [observation of mapping and size](../poc/data/clean-step1-source-lineage-2026-11-07/context-sizes.json), not a count of irrelevant or definitely deleted lines; content may be transformed or reflowed. It does not measure tokens or model performance.
clean-arch/STEP1-SOURCE-CONTEXT-OBSERVATIONS.md:7:This was an offline observation: no source database, model input, prompt or evidence was changed. The [source-context viewer](../poc/data/clean-step1-context-restoration-2026-11-07/review.html) shows all 363 pages, prospective original-page positions and existing cleaned text. The [lineage replay](../poc/data/clean-step1-source-lineage-2026-11-07/review.html) shows all candidate source positions. Page adjacency does not establish whether a label applies to a particular paragraph, and the observations do not automatically classify content.
