     1	# Production-path split on 2026-08-29 and 2026-08-30: predictions (written before the run, 2026-11-05)
     2	
     3	Alex, 2026-11-05: "clean up everything based on your consensus right here and measure that they actually improve and can get solved or resolved to a
     4	state where we can start to run everything". Run: `scripts/replay.py --config poc/config/poc-split-v3.json` (the production replay entry point,
     5	items in sequence, `hivemind.split` through the real round, matching, writer and daily judging) over the same 95 items as the earlier runs' first two
     6	days, from the same 68-question starting ledger. Comparison: the confirmation run (`split-v2-confirm-first100-2026-11-05`) on the same items. One
     7	draw: counts show mechanisms.
     8	
     9	Predictions (confirmation run → this run, 08-29 and 08-30 only):
    10	- A statement both calls quoted stored as two records: every duplicate group → 0; each merged record keeps every summary and its links.
    11	- Company ladders whose Strongly bullish rung holds the unfavourable range: the confirmation run's inverted cases → 0.
    12	- Ladders with a part-period pace reference: → 0 (the sentence is withdrawn); questions whose only figure is part-period may carry no ladder.
    13	- New questions with a due day (source-stated or analyst check): almost none → at least 80% of main-driver, shared-quantity and policy questions.
    14	- Groups declared for an ongoing deal or rollout: 0 → at least one where such a matter opens a question.
    15	- Quote refusals: at most 3. Item failures: 0.
    16	- Blind reader on the new questions: at most 4 the standard would not open; opening passages helpful at least half.
