codex
**Do not freeze the 414 count.** I checked all 40 entries. The rule misses some articles shown to readers and also excludes articles found only in automated checks. D669 makes actual use the test. [D669](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/DECISIONS-log.md:9545) · [Location list](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-17-product-comparison/stage0/not-reads-list.md:1)

| List lines | Verdict |
|---|---|
| 1–4 | **Agree.** The four archive members are superseded corpus databases. [Backup inventory](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-10-25-english/data-manifest.md:56) |
| 5–7 | **Agree.** The two split-run databases each store 34,082 rows. The runs processed 95 August articles apiece. `poc/corpus/items.sqlite` is the assembled corpus. [Split run](/Users/lchingen/hivemind-no-preseed-evidence-review/poc/data/split-v3-prod-0829-0830-2026-11-05/predictions.md:3) · [Corpus builder](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/poc/corpus/README.md:6) |
| 8 | **Agree.** The lineage manifest lists eligible and selected IDs before the offline check runs. [Producer](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/poc/data/clean-step1-source-lineage-2026-11-07/probe.py:80) |
| 15–30 | **Agree.** These are selection records or staged inputs in SQLite’s `run` table. The separate `trace` table confirms 10 completed September articles for acceptance and four in each Flash run. Those reads already count. [Selection writer](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/clean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/select_fresh.py:100) · [Trace writer](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/clean-arch/step1/runner.py:259) |
| 39–40 | **Disagree.** Both contain the three selected D369 pilot texts. The manifest maps the September 13 original to its archived variant, and the reader checked all three originals against 18 answers. This article already has other read hits. [Builder](/Users/lchingen/hivemind-no-preseed-evidence-review/docs/research/2026-11-05-real-input-evidence/build_archived_variants.py:154) · [Reader report](/Users/lchingen/hivemind-no-preseed-evidence-review/docs/research/2026-11-05-real-input-evidence/existing-library-trace-review.zh.md:3) |
| 9, 13–14, 38 | **Agree.** These hold token counts, HTML structure, provenance counts and IDs, or an offline cleaner comparison. I found no evidence that their in-window rows supplied article text to a reader. [Page budget](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/poc/data/clean-step1-source-loss-census-2026-11-07/page_budget.py:12) · [Source-check report](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/clean-arch/STEP1-SOURCE-LOSS-CENSUS.md:26) |
| 10–12, 31–37 | **Disagree with the blanket exemption.** Readers inspected excerpts from the candidate, extractor and HTML comparisons, both symbol diffs, both Unicode diffs, the context samples, and the empty-key results. Count the articles whose excerpts were shown. For example, HTML v2 row 296 was reviewed and is still kept. [HTML review](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/poc/data/clean-step1-source-loss-council-2026-11-07/round3-response.md:16) · [Context read](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/poc/data/clean-step1-source-loss-council-2026-11-07/round1.jsonl:518) · [Diff and empty-key reads](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/poc/data/clean-step1-source-loss-council-2026-11-07/round2.jsonl:156) |

**Overcount of at least 10:** The lineage data, context observations and their two generated viewers are bulk-check outputs. The recorded content review used 30 fixed packets. I found 37 scored articles whose only current read hits are those four bulk files and which appear in none of the packets. Use the actual reader records to decide exposure. [Offline lineage check](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/clean-arch/STEP1-SOURCE-PROVENANCE-CENSUS.md:28) · [Context review](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/clean-arch/STEP1-SOURCE-CONTEXT-OBSERVATIONS.md:16)

DISAGREE: count the D369 pilot and reviewed excerpts, and remove bulk lineage and context hits where no actual read is recorded.
